WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.507
In under two minutes, you will change your contest's dates and details.

00:00:04.507 --> 00:00:05.648
We start on the map.

00:00:06.548 --> 00:00:09.834
Open your web browser, and go to SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:12.271 --> 00:00:14.703
This is the SoCal Lights home page.

00:00:14.703 --> 00:00:17.202
A message asks to use your location.

00:00:17.202 --> 00:00:18.552
Tap Use my location.

00:00:20.376 --> 00:00:22.744
Your browser asks for permission.

00:00:22.744 --> 00:00:23.441
Tap Allow.

00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:30.383
Look at the top right corner of the map.

00:00:30.383 --> 00:00:31.538
See the three dots?

00:00:31.538 --> 00:00:32.057
Tap them.

00:00:35.682 --> 00:00:37.574
In the menu, tap Contests.

00:00:39.393 --> 00:00:39.991
Tap Mine.

00:00:39.991 --> 00:00:41.843
These are the contests you run.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.435
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:45.435 --> 00:00:46.723
This is your dashboard.

00:00:48.658 --> 00:00:51.099
On the Overview, find Schedule.

00:00:51.099 --> 00:00:52.396
Tap Change dates.

00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:57.615
Change the date that entries close, and the voting dates.

00:01:01.371 --> 00:01:05.480
You can also change the name, the message, the prize, and the rules.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:07.385
Entrants see changes right away.

00:01:08.287 --> 00:01:09.579
Tap Save changes.

00:01:09.579 --> 00:01:13.744
The team is emailed about changes, so nobody is surprised.

00:01:15.692 --> 00:01:17.608
Next up: Run voting.
